// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Lampshade Hanging
// @category Metafiction / Narrative Devices
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Lampshade_Hanging
// @domain   Narrative
// @scale    scene
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): the writer defuses a threat to suspension of disbelief by having a character
// CALL ATTENTION to the implausible element — and then moving on. FRONTIER: a scene-scale metafictional
// tool — one beat. The discriminator is a [+Contrived] element bound on the `element=` role of a
// [&Lampshades] event; a character names the implausibility out loud. Distinct from Breaking the Fourth
// Wall (which addresses the audience): here the remark stays in-story, aimed at the contrivance itself.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"

assoc lampshade_hanging -> [
  fourth_wall : "leans on, without fully breaking, the",
  genre_savvy : "often voiced by a character who is"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// — founded here (the acknowledged contrivance is the discriminator; promotion model) —
prop Contrived     [+Narrative]      // an implausible element that threatens suspension of disbelief
verb Lampshades(element) [+Narrative] // calls attention to a contrivance, then moves on

imply LampshadeHanging -> [Metafictional, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Naming rule (scene scale): a character LAMPSHADES a [+Contrived] element — the implausibility bound on
// the `element=` role of a [&Lampshades] event (agent=$x), so phase-2 re-checks [+Contrived] on the bound
// element (STYLE §8). One beat: the contrivance is named and the story carries on. Binding the
// implausibility on the acknowledgment is the discriminator.
rule Lampshade_Hanging {
  when:
    obj  $thing [+Contrived]
    evt  $note [&Lampshades(agent=$x, element=$thing)]
  then:
    $note [+LampshadeHanging]
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Avengers: Age of Ultron — Hawkeye on the bridge (film, 2015) ===
// Mid-battle, pinned in a ruined building above a floating city as killer robots swarm, Hawkeye turns to
// the terrified girl beside him and says it for the audience: "The city is flying, we're fighting an army
// of robots, and I have a bow and arrow. None of this makes sense." He names exactly how absurd the
// premise is — and then shrugs, "but I'm going back out there because it's my job," and goes. The
// implausibility acknowledged, the story moves on.

// HAWKEYE — who says the absurd part out loud
char hawkeye [+Protagonist]

// THE ABSURD PREMISE — a flying city, a robot army, a man with a bow
obj the_absurd_premise [+Contrived]

// INT. RUINED BUILDING - the floating city beyond the window
set the_ruin [+Interior]

scene the_pep_talk {
  beat 1 {
    hawkeye @ the_ruin
    // he names how little sense the premise makes — then goes back out anyway
    evt the_lampshade [&Lampshades(agent=hawkeye, element=the_absurd_premise)]
    // Lampshade_Hanging -> the_lampshade [+LampshadeHanging]
  }
}
